# Canonicalises author identities for `git log`, `git shortlog` and `git blame`.
#
# Rewrites nothing: git applies this at read time, so every commit SHA and the
# published history on main stay exactly as they are. GitHub's web UI ignores
# mailmap, so this fixes local history views only.
#
# Four identities accumulated across this repo's history, all the same person:
#
#   Manish Kumar Soni <144194721+Mu0810@users.noreply.github.com>  (6 commits)
#   Mu0810            <144194721+Mu0810@users.noreply.github.com>  (2)
#   Mu0810            <Mu0810@users.noreply.github.com>            (1, legacy
#                       noreply form without the account-id prefix)
#   hello             <hello@hellos-MacBook-Air.local>             (1, a machine
#                       fallback -- an account name plus a hostname, which
#                       GitHub cannot link to any account)
#
# The two-argument form below maps *any* commit carrying the listed email to the
# canonical name and email, whatever name that commit recorded -- so it covers
# the "Mu0810" and "hello" name variants without needing an entry each.
#
# Deliberately NOT mapped: Kiro Agent
# <244629292+kiro-agent@users.noreply.github.com>. Those commits were authored by
# an agent, not by Manish, and collapsing them here would claim work under the
# wrong name in the opposite direction.

Manish Kumar Soni <0810sonimanish@gmail.com> <144194721+Mu0810@users.noreply.github.com>
Manish Kumar Soni <0810sonimanish@gmail.com> <Mu0810@users.noreply.github.com>
Manish Kumar Soni <0810sonimanish@gmail.com> <hello@hellos-MacBook-Air.local>
